Port rivetit_sso from Odoo 19.0 to 20.0

Two incompatibilities blocked installation on Odoo 20:

1. Version. odoo/modules/module.py forces installable=False when the manifest
   version does not start with the running series, which surfaces as the
   misleading "AssertionError: Module not installable" even though the manifest
   says 'installable': True. Bumped 19.0.1.0.0 -> 20.0.1.0.0.
   (Declaring a 3-part version such as 1.0.0 would instead let Odoo prefix the
   running series automatically, making the module series-agnostic.)

2. Security. Odoo 20 removed the ir.model.access model in favour of ir.access.
   Renamed security/ir.model.access.csv -> security/ir.access.csv, updated the
   manifest data list, and converted the columns: the four perm_* booleans
   collapse into a single "operation" value (a subset of crud), model_id takes
   the model name rather than an xml_id, and group_id becomes group_id/id.
   Also added the missing rule for rivetit.sso.code.

Verified on Odoo 20.0-20260926: module installs, both models register, both
ir.access rules load, menus and the cleanup cron are created, and the
controller serves live (POST /rivetit/sso/health returns its own 401 JSON).

